' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' --- What the part contracts to ---
'
' Every messaging type is a flat struct carrying a request, a response, or a
' shared payload. Each request names its reply through `using response_type`
' and carries `static constexpr std::string_view nats_subject`, so the subject
' and the reply type travel with the request and no caller spells either one.
'
' The part publishes twelve subjects in two families:
'
'   ore.v1.series_key_shapes.*            the canonical entity protocol
'   ore.v1.series_key_shapes_versions.*   the point-in-time reads
'   workflow.v1.ore.import                the import workflow trigger
'   ore.v1.ore.import.{execute,rollback}  the import saga steps
'
' The saga subjects double the component name. The entity family reads
' ore.v1.series_key_shapes.list; the saga reads ore.v1.ore.import.execute,
' which says "ore" twice.

ores::ore::messaging::list_series_key_shapes_request --> ores::ore::messaging::list_series_key_shapes_response : response_type
ores::ore::messaging::get_series_key_shape_request --> ores::ore::messaging::get_series_key_shape_response : response_type
ores::ore::messaging::put_series_key_shape_request --> ores::ore::messaging::put_series_key_shape_response : response_type
ores::ore::messaging::delete_series_key_shape_request --> ores::ore::messaging::delete_series_key_shape_response : response_type
ores::ore::messaging::list_series_key_shape_versions_request --> ores::ore::messaging::list_series_key_shape_versions_response : response_type
ores::ore::messaging::ore_import_request --> ores::ore::messaging::ore_import_response : response_type
ores::ore::messaging::ore_import_execute_request --> ores::ore::messaging::ore_import_execute_result : response_type

' The entity, its change payloads and its events are four views of one row.
ores::ore::messaging::series_key_shape_write ..> ores::ore::domain::series_key_shape : carries
ores::ore::messaging::series_key_shape_change ..> ores::ore::domain::series_key_shape : carries
ores::ore::messaging::list_series_key_shapes_response ..> ores::ore::domain::series_key_shape : returns
ores::ore::eventing::series_key_shape_changed_event ..> ores::ore::messaging::series_key_shape_change : carries

' --- What the automated pass cannot see ---
'
' Three things in this part have no class to hang off, so they are absent from
' the picture above and from every picture the generator will produce:
'
'   include/ores.ore.api/workflow/ore_import_workflow.hpp
'       register_ore_import_workflow(registry). ores.workflow.core calls it
'       from its registrar, which is the one place another component reaches
'       into this part.
'   include/ores.ore.api/generators/series_key_shape_generator.hpp
'       generate_synthetic_series_key_shape(s), the sample rows the entity
'       integration test uses.
'   include/ores.ore.api/export.hpp
'       the visibility macros; the part builds a shared library.
'
' The .cpp files under src/ build ores.ore.api.lib, so the part is not
' header-only even though the diagram shows only declarations.

